<title>USA: Nu Skin sees benefits from price hikes.</title>
<headline>Nu Skin sees benefits from price hikes.</headline>
<dateline>PROVO, Utah 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nu Skin Asia Pacific Inc said it expects operations to be &quot;positively impacted&quot; by the previously announced five- to nine-percent price increases planned for Japan, Taiwan, South Korea and Hong Kong during the second quarter.</p>
<p>The increases should lead to increased gross profit margins in future quarters, the company said.</p>
<p>Chief executive Steven Lund said he expects revenue growth in Japan and Taiwan to continue through natural business expansion and additional product introductions in each quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The company reported that revenues in the first quarter rose 70 percent to $211.0 million from $124.2 million, and net income grew 39 percent to $20.5 million, or $0.24 per share, compared with $14.8 million, or $0.18 per share.</p>
